        {
          "id": "691e0edd88d826e1f614d561",
          "question": "<p>A proton of mass \\( 1.67 \\times 10^{-27} \\mathrm{~kg} \\) and charge \\( 1.6 \\times 10^{-19} \\mathrm{C} \\) is projected with a speed of \\( 2 \\times 10^{6} \\) \\( \\mathrm{m} / \\mathrm{s} \\) at an angle of \\( 60^{\\circ} \\) to the \\( x \\)-axis. If a uniform magnetic field of \\( 0.104 \\mathrm{~T} \\) is applied along the \\( \\mathrm{y} \\) axis, the path of the proton is :</p>",
          "image_url": null,
          "images": [],
          "type": "mcq",
          "options": [
            "<p>A circle of radius \\( 0.2 \\mathrm{~m} \\) and time period of \\(&nbsp; \\pi \\times 10^{-7} \\mathrm{~s} \\)</p>",
            "<p>A circle of radius \\( 0.1 \\mathrm{~m} \\) and time period of \\( 2 \\pi \\times 10^{-7} \\mathrm{~s} \\)</p>",
            "<p>A helix of radius \\( 0.1 \\mathrm{~m} \\) and time period of \\( 2 \\pi \\times 10^{-7} \\mathrm{~s} \\)</p>",
            "<p>A helix of radius of \\( 0.2 \\mathrm{~m} \\) and time period \\( 4 \\pi \\times 10^{-7} \\mathrm{~s} \\)</p>"
          ],
          "correct": 2,
          "explanation": "<p>Path will be a helix</p>\n<p>By using <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>m</mi><mi>v</mi><mtext>&thinsp;</mtext><mi>sin</mi><mtext>&thinsp;</mtext><mi>&theta;</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mi>B</mi></mrow></mfrac></math></p>\n<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&rArr;</mo><mtext>&thinsp;</mtext><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1.67</mn><mtext>&thinsp;</mtext><mo>&times;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>&minus;</mo><mn>27</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&times;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&times;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>6</mn></msup><mo>&times;</mo><mi>sin</mi><mn>30</mn><mo>&deg;</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1.6</mn><mtext>&thinsp;</mtext><mo>&times;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>&minus;</mo><mn>19</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&times;</mo><mn>0.104</mn></mrow></mfrac></math></p>\n<p>= 0.1 m</p>\n<p>and its time period</p>\n<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>&pi;</mi><mi>m</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mi>B</mi></mrow></mfrac></math></p>\n<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mtext>&thinsp;</mtext><mo>&times;</mo><mtext>&thinsp;</mtext><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&pi;</mi><mo>&times;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>67</mn><mtext>&thinsp;</mtext><mo>&times;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>&minus;</mo><mn>27</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>6</mn><mtext>&thinsp;</mtext><mo>&times;</mo><mtext>&thinsp;</mtext><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>&minus;</mo><mn>19</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&times;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>104</mn></mrow></mfrac><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&pi;</mi><mtext>&thinsp;</mtext><mo>&times;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>&minus;</mo><mn>7</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo></mrow></msup><mi>S</mi><mi>e</mi><mi>c</mi></math>&nbsp;</p>"
        },
        {
          "id": "691e0edd88d826e1f614d559",
          "question": "<p>A proton (mass \\( =1.67 \\times 10^{-27} \\mathrm{~kg} \\) and charge \\( =1.6 \\times \\) \\( 10^{-19} \\mathrm{C} \\) ) enters perpendicular to a magnetic field of intensity <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn></math> weber \\( / \\mathrm{m}^{2} \\) with a velocity \\( 3.4 \\times 10^{7} \\mathrm{~m} / \\mathrm{sec} \\). The acceleration of the proton should be</p>",
          "image_url": null,
          "images": [],
          "type": "mcq",
          "options": [
            "<p>\\( 6.5 \\times 10^{15} \\mathrm{~m} / \\mathrm{sec}^{2} \\)</p>",
            "<p>\\( 6.5 \\times 10^{13} \\mathrm{~m} / \\mathrm{sec}^{2} \\)</p>",
            "<p>\\( 6.5 \\times 10^{11} \\mathrm{~m} / \\mathrm{sec}^{2} \\)</p>",
            "<p>\\( 6.5 \\times 10^{9} \\mathrm{~m} / \\mathrm{sec}^{2} \\)</p>"
          ],
          "correct": 0,
          "explanation": "<p>As we know that</p>\n<p><em>F</em> =&nbsp;<em>ma</em></p>\n<p><em>qvB</em>sin90&deg; =&nbsp;<em>ma</em></p>\n<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>q</mi><mi>v</mi><mi>B</mi></mrow><mi>m</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>&times;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>19</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&times;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&times;</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>&times;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>6</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>67</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mo>&times;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>27</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac></math></p>\n<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&times;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>15</mn></msup><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>s</mi><mi>e</mi><mi>c</mi></math></p>"
        },
        {
          "id": "691e0edd88d826e1f614d54e",
          "question": "<p>An electron moves in a circular orbit with a uniform speed ( v ). It produces a magnetic field ( B ) at the centre of the circle. The radius of the circle is proportional to;</p>",
          "image_url": null,
          "images": [],
          "type": "mcq",
          "options": [
            "<p>\\( \\dfrac{B}{v} \\)</p>",
            "<p>\\( \\dfrac{v}{B} \\)</p>",
            "<p>\\( \\sqrt{\\dfrac{v}{B}} \\)</p>",
            "<p>\\( \\sqrt{\\dfrac{B}{v}} \\)</p>"
          ],
          "correct": 2,
          "explanation": "<p><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>&#956;</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>R</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>&#956;</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mi>e</mi><mi>&#965;</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mi>&#960;</mi><msup><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></math></span></p>\n<p><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>{</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>e</mi><mi>&#965;</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>&#960;</mi><mi>R</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>}</mo></math></span></p>"
        },
        {
          "id": "691e0edd88d826e1f614d536",
          "question": "<p>A proton and an alpha particle are separately projected in a region where a uniform magnetic field exists. The initial velocities are perpendicular to the direction of magnetic field. If both the particles move along circles of equal radii, the ratio of momentum of proton to alpha particle \\( \\left(\\frac{P_{p}}{P_{\\alpha}}\\right) \\) is</p>",
          "image_url": null,
          "images": [],
          "type": "mcq",
          "options": [
            "<p>\\( 1 \\)</p>",
            "<p>\\( 1 / 2 \\)</p>",
            "<p>&nbsp;\\( 2 \\)</p>",
            "<p>\\( 1 / 4 \\)</p>"
          ],
          "correct": 1,
          "explanation": "<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>m</mi><mi>v</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mi>B</mi></mrow></mfrac></math></p>\n<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>q</mi><mi>B</mi></mrow></mfrac></math></p>\n<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>&#945;</mi></msub></math></p>\n<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mi>B</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>&#945;</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>&#945;</mi></msub><mi>B</mi></mrow></mfrac></math></p>\n<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>&#945;</mi></msub></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>&#945;</mi></msub></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>q</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>q</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math></p>"
        },
        {
          "id": "691e0edd88d826e1f614d54b",
          "question": "<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">A proton and an \\( \\alpha \\)-particle enter in a uniform magnetic field perpendicularly with same speed. The ratio of time periods of both particles \\( \\left(\\frac{T_{p}}{T_{\\alpha}}\\right) \\) will be;</p>",
          "image_url": null,
          "images": [],
          "type": "mcq",
          "options": [
            "<p>\\( 1: 2 \\)</p>",
            "<p>\\( 1: 3 \\)</p>",
            "<p>\\( 2: 1 \\)</p>",
            "<p>\\( 3: 1 \\)</p>"
          ],
          "correct": 0,
          "explanation": "<p>By using</p>\n<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>&#960;</mi><mi>m</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mi>B</mi></mrow></mfrac></math></p>\n<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mtext>&#8201;</mtext><mfrac><msub><mi>T</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#945;</mi></msub><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>p</mi></msub></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>m</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#945;</mi></msub><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>p</mi></msub></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><msub><mi>q</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#945;</mi></msub></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>p</mi></msub></mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>p</mi></msub></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mrow><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>p</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></math></p>\n<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mtext>&#8201;</mtext><msub><mi>T</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#945;</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>p</mi></msub></math></p>\n<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><msub><mi>T</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#945;</mi></msub></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math></p>"
        },
        {
          "id": "691e0edd88d826e1f614d548",
          "question": "<p>An electron and a proton are moving along the same direction with the same kinetic energy. They enter a uniform magnetic field acting perpendicular to their velocities. The dependence of radius of their path on their masses is:</p>",
