        {
          "id": "691e0edd88d826e1f614d56f",
          "question": "<p>A small circular loop of conducting wire has radius a and carries current \\(I\\). It is placed in a uniform magnetic field \\(B\\) perpendicular to its plane such that when rotated slightly about its diameter and released, it starts performing simple harmonic motion of time period \\(T\\). If the mass of the loop is \\(m\\) then:</p>",
          "image_url": null,
          "images": [],
          "type": "mcq",
          "options": [
            "<p>\\(T=\\sqrt{\\frac{\\pi m}{I B}}\\)</p>",
            "<p>\\(T=\\sqrt{\\frac{\\pi m}{2 I B}}\\)</p>",
            "<p>\\(T=\\sqrt{\\frac{2 \\pi m}{I B}}\\)</p>",
            "<p>\\(T=\\sqrt{\\frac{2 m}{I B}}\\)</p>"
          ],
          "correct": 2,
          "explanation": "<p>Torque on the loop, \\(\\tau=M B \\sin \\theta=I \\alpha\\)<br />[ \\(I\\) is moment of inertia of the loop about its diameter]<br />\\[<br />\\begin{aligned}<br />&amp; \\pi R^2 I B \\theta=\\frac{m R^2}{2} \\alpha \\\\<br />&amp; \\omega=\\sqrt{\\frac{2 \\pi I B}{m}}=\\frac{2 \\pi}{T} ; T=\\sqrt{\\frac{2 \\pi m}{I B}}<br />\\end{aligned}<br />\\]</p>"
        },
        {
          "id": "691e0edd88d826e1f614d556",
          "question": "<p>A neutron, a proton, an electron and an \\( \\alpha \\)-particle enters a uniform magnetic field with equal velocities. The field is directed along the inward normal to the plane of the paper. Which of these tracks is followed by \\( \\alpha \\)-particle.</p>\n<p><img title=\"19.JPG\" src=\"https://d2bps9p1kiy4ka.cloudfront.net/5b09189f7285894d9130ccd0/l5c9wff6su2e12x3azn9garsd.JPG\" alt=\"\" width=\"215\" height=\"178\" /></p>",
