        {
          "id": "691e0edd88d826e1f614d57a",
          "question": "<p>A uniform magnetic field acts at right angles to the direction of motion of electrons. As a result, the electron moves in a circular path of radius \\( 2 \\mathrm{~cm} \\). If the speed of the electrons is doubled, then the radius of the circular path will be</p>",
          "image_url": null,
          "images": [],
          "type": "mcq",
          "options": [
            "<p>\\( 2.0 \\mathrm{~cm} \\)</p>",
            "<p>\\( 0.5 \\mathrm{~cm} \\)</p>",
            "<p>\\( 4.0 \\mathrm{~cm} \\)</p>",
            "<p>\\( 1.0 \\mathrm{~cm} \\)</p>"
          ],
          "correct": 2,
          "explanation": "<p>For motion perpendicular to a uniform <span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">B</annotation></semantics></math></span>-field,</p>\n<p><span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"block\"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>m</mi><mi>v</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mi>B</mi></mrow></mfrac><mspace width=\"1em\"></mspace><mtext>(radius&nbsp;&prop;&nbsp;speed)</mtext><mo>:</mo><mi>c</mi><mi>o</mi><mi>n</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>e</mi><mi>n</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>R</mi><mi>e</mi><mi>f</mi><mi>e</mi><mi>r</mi><mi>e</mi><mi>n</mi><mi>c</mi><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">[</mo><mi>o</mi><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>e</mi><mo>:</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">]</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mi>n</mi><mi>d</mi><mi>e</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">.</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">r=\\frac{mv}{qB}\\quad\\text{(radius &prop; speed)}:contentReference[oaicite:0]{index=0}.</annotation></semantics></math></span></p>\n<p>Doubling <span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">v</annotation></semantics></math></span> doubles <span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">r</annotation></semantics></math></span>: <span class=\"katex\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mtext>  </mtext><mtext>cm</mtext><mo>&rarr;</mo><mn>4</mn><mtext>  </mtext><mtext>cm</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">2\\;\\text{cm} \\to 4\\;\\text{cm}</annotation></semantics></math></span>.</p>"
