    {
      "name": "DPP 05",
      "displayName": "DPP 05",
      "questions": [
        {
          "id": "69266e40a6d38edcb17cb2e2",
          "question": "<p>A rectangular coil \\( \\mathrm{PQ} \\) has \\( 2 \\mathrm{n} \\) turns, an area \\( 2 \\mathrm{a} \\) and carries a current \\( 2 I \\), (refer figure). The plane of the coil is at \\( 60^{\\circ} \\) to a horizontal uniform magnetic field of flux density \\( \\mathrm{B}\\). The torque on the coil due to magnetic force is</p>\n<p><img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"https://penpencil-static-content.s3.ap-south-1.amazonaws.com/5eb393ee95fab7468a79d189/wqrlylxqo9jyohifvmga4nwmh.png\" /></p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>",
          "image_url": "https://penpencil-static-content.s3.ap-south-1.amazonaws.com/5eb393ee95fab7468a79d189/wqrlylxqo9jyohifvmga4nwmh.png",
          "images": [
            "https://penpencil-static-content.s3.ap-south-1.amazonaws.com/5eb393ee95fab7468a79d189/wqrlylxqo9jyohifvmga4nwmh.png"
          ],
          "type": "mcq",
          "options": [
            "<p>\\( \\mathrm{Bna} I \\sin 60^{\\circ} \\)</p>",
            "<p>\\( 8 \\mathrm{Bna} I \\cos 60^{\\circ} \\)</p>",
            "<p>\\( 4 \\mathrm{na} I \\mathrm{~B} \\sin 60^{\\circ} \\)</p>",
            "<p>none</p>"
          ],
          "correct": 1
        },
        {
          "id": "69266e40a6d38edcb17cb2df",
          "question": "<p>A small coil of \\( N \\) turns has area \\( A \\) and a current \\( I \\) flows through it. The magnetic dipole moment of this coil will be</p>",
          "image_url": null,
          "images": [],
          "type": "mcq",
          "options": [
            "<p>II \\( A \\)</p>",
            "<p>\\( N I^{2} A \\)</p>",
            "<p>\\( N^{2} A I \\)</p>",
            "<p>NIA</p>"
          ],
          "correct": 3
        },
        {
          "id": "69266e40a6d38edcb17cb2dc",
          "question": "<p>Consider a tightly wound coil of radius \\(20 cm\\) having 200 turns and carrying a current of \\(2 A\\). The magnitude of the magnetic field at the centre of the coil is</p>",
          "image_url": null,
          "images": [],
          "type": "mcq",
          "options": [
            "<p>\\(4 \\pi \\times 10^{-4} T\\)</p>",
            "<p>\\(2 \\pi \\times 10^{-4} T\\)</p>",
            "<p>\\(4 \\pi \\times 10^{-3} T\\)</p>",
            "<p>&nbsp;\\(4 \\pi \\times 10^{-2} T\\)</p>"
          ],
          "correct": 0,
          "explanation": "<p>Answer (1)<br />Since coil is tightly wound, we may take each circular element to have same radius.<br />\\[<br />\\begin{aligned}<br />&amp; h=20 cm =0.2 m , N=200 \\\\<br />&amp; B=\\frac{\\mu_0 N I}{2 R}=\\frac{4 \\pi \\times 10^{-7} \\times 200 \\times 2}{2 \\times 0.2} \\\\<br />&amp; B=4 \\pi \\times 10^{-4} T<br />\\end{aligned}<br />\\]</p>"
        },
        {
          "id": "69266e40a6d38edcb17cb2d9",
          "question": "<p>A tightly wound long solenoid has \\( n \\) turns per unit length, radius \\( r \\) and carries a current \\( i \\). A particle having charge \\( q \\) and mass \\( m \\) is projected from a point on the axis in the direction perpendicular to the axis. The maximum speed for which particle does not strike the solenoid will be</p>",
          "image_url": null,
          "images": [],
          "type": "mcq",
          "options": [
            "<p>\\( \\frac{\\mu_{0} q r n i}{2 m} \\)</p>",
            "<p>\\( \\frac{\\mu_{0} q r n i}{m} \\)</p>",
            "<p>\\( \\frac{2 \\mu_{0} q r n i}{3 m} \\)</p>",
            "<p>None of these</p>"
          ],
          "correct": 0
        },
        {
          "id": "69266e40a6d38edcb17cb2d0",
          "question": "<p>Ampere circuital law is given by \\( \\oint \\overrightarrow{\\mathrm{B}} \\overrightarrow{\\mathrm{d}} \\mathrm{l}=\\mu_{0} \\mathrm{l} \\) inside for a closed loop. Now choose the correct alternative</p>",
          "image_url": null,
          "images": [],
          "type": "mcq",
          "options": [
            "<p>Magnetic field is due to all the current element inside as well as outside the loop</p>",
            "<p>Magnetic field is only due to the current element outside the loop</p>",
            "<p>Magnetic field is only due to the current element inside the loop</p>",
            "<p>Magnetic field is only due to the current element passing through the loop</p>"
          ],
          "correct": 0,
          "explanation": "<p>The magnetic field <strong>B</strong> at any point on the loop is the vector sum of contributions from <strong>all</strong> current elements, whether they are inside or outside the loop. so that's why Option (A) will correct <strong>Magnetic field is due to all the current element inside as well as outside the loop .</strong></p>"
        },
        {
          "id": "69266e40a6d38edcb17cb2f1",
